6939655172413792, "no_speech_prob": 0.053800374269485474}, {"id": 51, "seek": 23560, "start": 240.48, "end": 246.51999999999998, "text": " And then we all obviously have this like hierarchy of PD arrays where rejection block is the", "tokens": [50608, 400, 550, 321, 439, 2745, 362, 341, 411, 22333, 295, 10464, 41011, 689, 26044, 3461, 307, 264, 50910], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.25194744072338143, "compression_ratio": 1.6939655172413792, "no_speech_prob": 0.053800374269485474}, {"id": 52, "seek": 23560, "start": 246.51999999999998, "end": 247.51999999999998, "text": " most discounted one.", "tokens": [50910, 881, 11635, 292, 472, 13, 50960], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.25194744072338143, "compression_ratio": 1.6939655172413792, "no_speech_prob": 0.053800374269485474}, {"id": 53, "seek": 23560, "start": 247.51999999999998, "end": 254.2, "text": " And we can see this down here on this four hour rejection block gets tapped, right?", "tokens": [50960, 400, 321, 393, 536, 341, 760, 510, 322, 341, 1451, 1773, 26044, 3461, 2170, 38693, 11, 558, 30, 51294], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.25194744072338143, "compression_ratio": 1.6939655172413792, "no_speech_prob": 0.053800374269485474}, {"id": 54, "seek": 23560, "start": 254.2, "end": 256.2, "text": " That is the first area that gets formed.", "tokens": [51294, 663, 307, 264, 700, 1859, 300, 2170, 8693, 13, 51394], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.25194744072338143, "compression_ratio": 1.6939655172413792, "no_speech_prob": 0.053800374269485474}, {"id": 55, "seek": 23560, "start": 256.2, "end": 261.2, "text": " And then we can see this four hour change instead of delivery or CISD.", "tokens": [51394, 400, 550, 321, 393, 536, 341, 1451, 1773, 1319, 2602, 295, 8982, 420, 383, 2343, 35, 13, 51644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.25194744072338143, "compression_ratio": 1.6939655172413792, "no_speech_prob": 0.053800374269485474}, {"id": 56, "seek": 23560, "start": 261.2, "end": 265.08, "text": " This gets formed and tapped into, right?", "tokens": [51644, 639, 2170, 8693, 293, 38693, 666, 11, 558, 30, 51838], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.25194744072338143, "compression_ratio": 1.6939655172413792, "no_speech_prob": 0.053800374269485474}, {"id": 57, "seek": 26508, "start": 265.08, "end": 269.12, "text": " And then we have a fair value gap, which gets formed.", "tokens": [50364, 400, 550, 321, 362, 257, 3143, 2158, 7417, 11, 597, 2170, 8693, 13, 50566], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23994521020163953, "compression_ratio": 1.53125, "no_speech_prob": 0.003628900507465005}, {"id": 58, "seek": 26508, "start": 269.12, "end": 275.56, "text": " That's on this by side leg, the by side of the curve.", "tokens": [50566, 663, 311, 322, 341, 538, 1252, 1676, 11, 264, 538, 1252, 295, 264, 7605, 13, 50888], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23994521020163953, "compression_ratio": 1.53125, "no_speech_prob": 0.003628900507465005}, {"id": 59, "seek": 26508, "start": 275.56, "end": 279.8, "text": " And then we start forming inverse for value gaps.", "tokens": [50888, 400, 550, 321, 722, 15745, 17340, 337, 2158, 15031, 13, 51100], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23994521020163953, "compression_ratio": 1.53125, "no_speech_prob": 0.003628900507465005}, {"id": 60, "seek": 26508, "start": 279.8, "end": 283.15999999999997, "text": " And then we form breakers, right?", "tokens": [51100, 400, 550, 321, 1254, 1821, 433, 11, 558, 30, 51268], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23994521020163953, "compression_ratio": 1.53125, "no_speech_prob": 0.003628900507465005}, {"id": 61, "seek": 26508, "start": 283.15999999999997, "end": 289.36, "text": " So these are all like the hierarchy of the PD arrays.", "tokens": [51268, 407, 613, 366, 439, 411, 264, 22333, 295, 264, 10464, 41011, 13, 51578], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23994521020163953, "compression_ratio": 1.53125, "no_speech_prob": 0.003628900507465005}, {"id": 62, "seek": 28936, "start": 289.36, "end": 296.92, "text": " Next box, the most discounted ones, CISDs are the second most discounted ones, at least", "tokens": [50364, 3087, 2424, 11, 264, 881, 11635, 292, 2306, 11, 383, 2343, 35, 82, 366, 264, 1150, 881, 11635, 292, 2306, 11, 412, 1935, 50742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2914032220840454, "compression_ratio": 1.5344827586206897, "no_speech_prob": 0.35998421907424927}, {"id": 63, "seek": 28936, "start": 296.92, "end": 299.2, "text": " most of the time they are.", "tokens": [50742, 881, 295, 264, 565, 436, 366, 13, 50856], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2914032220840454, "compression_ratio": 1.5344827586206897, "no_speech_prob": 0.35998421907424927}, {"id": 64, "seek": 28936, "start": 299.2, "end": 302.04, "text": " This should be there's almost no way there aren't.", "tokens": [50856, 639, 820, 312, 456, 311, 1920, 572, 636, 456, 3212, 380, 13, 50998], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2914032220840454, "compression_ratio": 1.5344827586206897, "no_speech_prob": 0.35998421907424927}, {"id": 65, "seek": 28936, "start": 302.04, "end": 307.92, "text": " And then you got like IFEGs and then breakers, usually.", "tokens": [50998, 400, 550, 291, 658, 411, 26080, 36, 33715, 293, 550, 1821, 433, 11, 2673, 13, 51292], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2914032220840454, "compression_ratio": 1.5344827586206897, "no_speech_prob": 0.35998421907424927}, {"id": 66, "seek": 28936, "start": 307.92, "end": 314.6, "text": " So that pretty much covers it, I think, yeah.", "tokens": [51292, 407, 300, 1238, 709, 10538, 309, 11, 286, 519, 11, 1338, 13, 51626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2914032220840454, "compression_ratio": 1.5344827586206897, "no_speech_prob": 0.35998421907424927}], "language": "en"}